  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ac100-500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ac 102.08 CPA firm",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-07-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ac 102.08 “CPA firm” means “CPA firm” as defined by RSA 309-B:3, IV, namely, “a sole proprietorship, a corporation, a partnership including a limited liability partnership, a limited liability company including a professional limited liability company, or any other legally authorized association issued a license under RSA 309-B:8.”\n\nSource. #6901, eff 12-4-98; ss by #8810, INTERIM, eff 1-25-07, EXPIRED: 7-25-07\n\nNew. #9032, eff 11-21-07; ss by #10053, eff 1-1-12 (from Ac 101.07); renumbered by #13995 (formerly Ac 102.07)",
